                <h4>Population Health Management</h4>
                <p>Community detection algorithms reveal natural patient cohorts that can inform targeted public health interventions. These data-driven cohorts often align with clinical phenotypes but may reveal novel groupings that cut across traditional diagnostic categories, enabling more precise population segmentation for preventive programs and resource allocation.</p>

                <h4>Clinical Decision Support</h4>
                <p>Graph analytics provides clinical decision support by revealing contextual information not immediately apparent from individual patient records. Personalized PageRank suggests relevant comorbidities to monitor, pathway analysis highlights potential clinical trajectories, and similarity analysis identifies relevant peer groups for benchmarking and treatment planning.</p>

                <h4>Healthcare Operations Optimization</h4>
                <p>Organizational network analysis identifies structurally central healthcare providers and bridges between different care networks. This information supports healthcare referral optimization, identification of potential care coordination gaps, and strategic planning for healthcare network development and integration.</p>
